---
import Document from '../layouts/Document.astro';
import LinkButton from '../components/LinkButton';
import { Alert, AlertTitle, AlertDescription } from '../components/ui/alert';
import release from '../lib/release.json';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Document title="Download ZEC Buying Price for macOS" description={`Version ${site.version} development DMG for Apple Silicon and macOS 14+. Check the checksum, signing status, Secure Enclave protection, and known limits.`}>
  <Alert><AlertTitle>Version {site.version} · development build</AlertTitle><AlertDescription>{release.notarized ? 'This DMG is Developer ID signed and notarized by Apple, with a stapled notarization ticket.' : release.signed ? 'This DMG is Developer ID signed. It is not notarized by Apple; Gatekeeper acceptance has not been verified.' : 'Packaging and signing checks are pending.'} {release.gatekeeperVerified ? 'Gatekeeper verification passed.' : ''} Complete wallet scanning and reorg handling remain under verification.</AlertDescription></Alert>
  <p><LinkButton href="/download/" /></p>
  <ul><li>Released: 9 October 2026</li><li>Platform: Apple Silicon (arm64), macOS 14 or later; Secure Enclave required</li><li>Download size: {release.sizeMiB === null ? 'Pending packaging' : `${release.sizeMiB} MiB`}</li><li>Signing: {release.notarized ? 'Developer ID Application; Apple notarization ticket stapled' : release.signed ? 'Developer ID Application; hardened runtime and secure timestamp; not notarized' : 'Pending verification'}</li><li>Distribution: versioned GitHub prerelease asset</li></ul>
  <h2>Verify the download</h2>
  <p>SHA-256 for <code>{release.filename}</code>:</p>
  <pre tabindex="0"><code>{release.sha256 ?? 'Pending packaging'}</code></pre>
  <p>Run this command from the directory containing the downloaded file and compare the result:</p>
  <pre tabindex="0"><code>{`shasum -a 256 ${release.filename}`}</code></pre>
  <p><a href="/downloads/SHA256SUMS.txt">Download checksum file</a> · <a href={site.release}>View the GitHub release</a></p>
  <p>Previous 0.2.0 downloads remain available on the <a href="https://github.com/megabyte0x/zec-buyingprice/releases/tag/v0.2.0-dev">earlier GitHub release</a>. Use the filename and checksum above for this download.</p>
  <h2>What changed in 0.2.1?</h2>
  <p>Transactions now appear as the SDK discovers and enhances them during synchronization. Saved history appears when the worker starts. The acquisition value and average update from available data and carry a provisional label while scanning or pricing continues.</p>
  <p>Incoming snapshots preserve your saved selections and known prices, even while a historical-price request is running. Earlier receipts can recalculate the ledger as they arrive. Pending movements remain excluded, and selected sends must reconcile against selected receipts.</p>
  <p>The worker combines duplicate history-refresh requests, reuses a database connection and output query, and limits scan-metric reads to once per second. Historical prices are shared across movements on the same UTC day; failed dates wait for an explicit retry. Transactions with incomplete details are counted visibly while their classification is unresolved.</p>
  <p>The update follows Vizor’s transaction-driven refresh approach. It reduces application overhead; a full-sync speed improvement has not been benchmarked. The Swift SDK still controls scanning batches and its disk block cache.</p>
  <h2>Wallet protection retained from 0.2.0</h2>
  <p>Your viewing key is encrypted using Secure Enclave protection, and wallet history stays inside an AES-256 encrypted local volume. Touch ID or your Mac login password unlocks each new session. The viewing-only scanner runs in a separate worker process.</p>
  <p>Syncing continues while you switch apps, hide the app, or minimize its window; the wallet interface locks until you authenticate again. Closing the last wallet window, quitting, sleeping, or locking the Mac stops the worker and closes protected storage. A helper attempts storage cleanup if the app exits unexpectedly.</p>
  <p>The scan bar follows the SDK’s work percentage. Block details separately report completed blocks scanned, the chain tip, and continuous verified coverage. Newer ranges can be scanned first, so the verified height can pause while other work advances.</p>
  <p>The app also includes configurable TLS scanning, daily USD price estimates, movement selection, manual prices, and locally persisted choices. The package includes the Swift compatibility runtime needed by its executable.</p>
  <h2>Current verification limits</h2>
  <p>The updated executable builds and launches. One focused regression test passed for progressive snapshots, retained prices and selections, and running acquisition-value recalculation. Native unlock and background synchronization were observed in the earlier security update. The earlier implementation had 18 passing accounting and selected SDK integration tests; the full suite has not been rerun for this release.</p>
  <p>Last-window close and quit cleanup, crash cleanup, migration, complete receipt/spend scanning, interruption/resume, and controlled reorg behavior remain under verification. Synthetic screenshots do not establish full scan completion. Developer ID app and DMG signatures and disk-image integrity checks passed. {release.notarized ? 'Apple notarization was accepted and its ticket was stapled and validated.' : 'Apple notarization has not been verified.'} {release.gatekeeperVerified ? 'Gatekeeper acceptance passed.' : 'Gatekeeper acceptance has not been verified.'} Distribution checks do not establish the correctness of acquisition calculations.</p>
  <h2>Install and inspect</h2>
  <p>Open the DMG and drag the app into Applications. Follow the <a href="/setup/">setup guide</a> for macOS opening guidance, authentication, and viewing-key import. The build is not a verified production release. Source revision: <code>{release.sourceRevision}</code>, built in the optimized release configuration with the compatibility library added during packaging.</p>
  <p>The app does not generate tax reports. Review <a href="/methodology/">calculation methodology</a> and <a href="/privacy/">privacy behavior</a> before using sensitive history.</p>
</Document>
